          "filename": "Staigue stone fort - geograph.org.uk - 1417778.jpg",
          "caption": "Staigue stone fort Staigue stone fort is a round stone iron-age fort near Sneem, probably built as a defensive stronghold for a local leader and his clan.\nThe walls are over 5m high in places, and up to 4m thick. It is an impressive construction, built without any sort of mortar.",
          "alt": "Staigue stone fort Staigue stone fort is a round stone iron-age fort near Sneem, probably built as a defensive stronghold for a local leader and his clan.\nThe walls are over 5m high in places, and up to 4m thick. It is an impressive construction, built without any sort of mortar.",
